WEBVTT

00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:15,380
A Sheba Global tested today at 7.9 and I'm scheduled for surgery in three weeks.

00:00:15,380 --> 00:00:21,900
They want to bring up my Heba Global either with a blood transfusion or supplementation.

00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:26,340
I know cancer cells can feed on iron, what would we recommend?

00:00:26,340 --> 00:00:31,300
I would recommend, if your Heba Global is 7.9, there's the fastest way to raise Heba Global

00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:33,220
is a blood transfusion.

00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:39,340
I mean, there's just that is there's just no substitute for that.

00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:42,060
So I would recommend that that will raise it up.

00:00:42,060 --> 00:00:46,140
That would because you're getting the influx of blood,

00:00:46,140 --> 00:00:49,180
you're not really feeding the cancer with that either.

00:00:49,180 --> 00:00:52,300
And yes, iron can feed cancer.

00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:57,300
If your Heba Global was at a point where they would not give you a blood transfusion,

00:00:57,300 --> 00:01:00,700
let's say it's 8.3 and their cutoff is 8.0.

00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:05,380
Different hospitals, different clinics have different cutoffs.

00:01:05,380 --> 00:01:09,860
So if they are willing to give you a blood transfusion, I would definitely go with that.

00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:14,540
So it's going to raise your Heba Global.

00:01:14,540 --> 00:01:19,260
Most rapidly, you'll feel a lot better, you'll be prepped for the surgery.

